From 6b887e9b6eca0ee18542b0dcbdf4a71763f0262d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:05:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: the hub CPU advisory names an unreadable
 pool limit; one measured census step count

Follow-up to PR #1863 (review t_01a1d3154dc65cfb's non-blocking nits; card t_01a1d32c4a18538a).

1. Switch interval: nothing to narrow. The reviewed head ca7e41506a ran the whole admission.lock hold at a 0.25 ms
   switch interval, including the ~1 s cpu.sample() wait. The landed 142553d6f0 was rebased onto cc9d41d953
   (one-statement census) and 6bd4b97b00 (the gate re-reads the sampler's sample, no sample under the lock) and
   carries no setswitchinterval at all; main's hold now has no sample wait to cover. Hub evidence (task_events,
   last 8 h): no hub_admission_overrun or final-gate refusal since the fix landed, hub_cpu_unknown last at 04:28Z,
   claims with hub_cpu evidence through 06:50Z. The CPU limit, cap and CLAIM_MAX_HOLD_S are unchanged.
2. The lock-free advisory returned hub_cpu_unknown both for its sample and when advisory_limit() raised (priority-pool
   settings or the card's admission class unreadable). The pool-limit failure now defers as
   hub_cpu_pool_limit_unknown (in kanban_queue_reason.CODES), so hub_cpu_unknown means the sample only (missing,
   stale, future-dated or malformed: a non-number field, busy % outside 0-100, window outside 1-2 s). The docstring,
   the reason-block comment and docs/worker-first-v1.md name every cause.
3. One measured census step count: on a copy of a real board (55-column tasks, 22-column task_runs, 8 running rows;
   the hub's kanban.db has the same 55/22 columns) the pre-cc9d41d953 census made 95 sqlite steps and main's
   one-statement census makes 4. machine_metrics (module comment and table_columns), the convoy and contention test
   docstrings now say 95 / 55 / 22 instead of ~80, ~70, ~840 and ~130.

Tests: test_kanban_hub_admission_guards::test_invalid_pool_policy_defers_at_advisory_before_lease now expects
hub_cpu_pool_limit_unknown; test_kanban_hub_gate_convoy adds the advisory pool-limit unit test and puts the new code
through the queue-line/CODES check; test_kanban_hub_admission's advisory pre-check adds malformed pct (150, "text")
cases that stay hub_cpu_unknown. RED on origin/main code (tests only): convoy fails at collection
(no HUB_CPU_POOL_LIMIT_UNKNOWN), guards 2 failed ('hub_cpu_unknown' == 'hub_cpu_pool_limit_unknown').
GREEN: 5 hub gate files 197 passed; 19 queue-reason/admission consumer files 465 passed; scripts/check ok.
